///1ED
Help by Willem Aandewiel
ED - Edit text with the CP/M line editor

///2STARTING
  E>A:ED NOTES.TXT

ED is a command-driven editor, not a full-screen editor.
Enter the following editing commands at the ED prompt.

///2NEWFILE
For a new file, enter I and press Return.
Type the required text lines.
Press Ctrl-Z to leave text-entry mode.
Enter E to save the changes and exit ED.
Ctrl-Z means the key combination, not the literal letters.

///2EXISTING
Read text from the existing file into the editing buffer:

  #A
  B
  #T

#A reads as much text as the buffer can hold.
B moves to the beginning. #T displays text from the current position.
A large file may not fit entirely in the buffer.

///2SAVING
E saves the result and exits ED.
Q abandons the current editing session without saving its changes;
answer any confirmation requested by your version.
Keep a backup first. ED normally uses a .BAK backup file.
Use ED for text, not for .COM files or other binary data.
